<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Multimodal on Best of AI</title><link>https://bestofai.io/tags/multimodal/</link><description>Recent content in Multimodal on Best of AI</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-US</language><lastBuildDate>Mon, 15 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://bestofai.io/tags/multimodal/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Minimax</title><link>https://bestofai.io/tools/minimax-ai/</link><pubDate>Mon, 15 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://bestofai.io/tools/minimax-ai/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Gemini</title><link>https://bestofai.io/tools/gemini/</link><pubDate>Sun, 21 Sep 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://bestofai.io/tools/gemini/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Gemini is Google&amp;rsquo;s answer to ChatGPT, and what sets it apart is how deeply it&amp;rsquo;s woven into products people already use every day. It sits inside Gmail to help draft and summarise emails, inside Google Docs to rewrite and restructure text, inside Google Meet to take notes, and inside Android to respond to voice queries. For anyone already living in the Google ecosystem, Gemini often shows up exactly where the work is happening rather than requiring a separate tab.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Gemini Advanced</title><link>https://bestofai.io/tools/gemini-advanced/</link><pubDate>Sun, 21 Sep 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://bestofai.io/tools/gemini-advanced/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Google AI Studio</title><link>https://bestofai.io/tools/google-ai-studio/</link><pubDate>Sun, 21 Sep 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://bestofai.io/tools/google-ai-studio/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Llama 3</title><link>https://bestofai.io/tools/llama-3/</link><pubDate>Sun, 21 Sep 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://bestofai.io/tools